From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Heikki Krogerus <heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:51:29 +0530
Subject: i2c: designware: Add quirk for Intel Xe

The xe driver registers the DesignWare I2C host controller as a platform
device whose parent is the GPU PCI device, and installs a regmap on that
parent which translates register accesses into GPU MMIO (with the required
Xe specific handling of DW_IC_ENABLE and friends). The controller has no
MMIO resource of its own, so devm_platform_ioremap_resource() cannot be
used.

When the platform device is marked compatible with "intel,xe-i2c", fetch
the regmap from the parent device instead of mapping a resource. velinux
i2c_dw_init_regmap() already honours a pre-populated dev->map, so no further
change is needed there.

device_is_compatible() is not available on velinux 5.15, so match the
"compatible" property directly via fwnode_property_match_string().

Signed-off-by: Heikki Krogerus heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20250701122252.2590230-3-heikki.krogerus@linux.intel.com
(backported from commit f6a8e9f3de4567c71ef9f5f13719df69a8b96081 linux-stable)
Signed-off-by: Nitin Gote nitin.r.gote@intel.com
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c
index eea51f91c1af..6aa5ab574d7d 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c
@@ -176,11 +176,30 @@ static void dw_i2c_plat_pm_cleanup(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
 		pm_runtime_put_noidle(dev->dev);
 }
 
+static int dw_i2c_get_parent_regmap(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
+{
+	dev->map = dev_get_regmap(dev->dev->parent, NULL);
+	if (!dev->map)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int dw_i2c_plat_request_regs(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
 {
 	struct platform_device *pdev = to_platform_device(dev->dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The Intel Xe I2C controller is a child of the GPU device and its
+	 * registers are reached through a regmap installed on the parent, so
+	 * take that regmap instead of mapping an MMIO resource.
+	 */
+	if (dev_fwnode(dev->dev) &&
+	    !fwnode_property_match_string(dev_fwnode(dev->dev), "compatible",
+					  "intel,xe-i2c"))
+		return dw_i2c_get_parent_regmap(dev);
+
 	switch (dev->flags & MODEL_MASK) {
 	case MODEL_BAIKAL_BT1:
 		ret = bt1_i2c_request_regs(dev);
-- 
